---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/global/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import HeroText from '../../components/hero/HeroText.astro';
import EvidenceGallery from '../../components/sections/EvidenceGallery.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/sections/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="House Extensions Leeds | WW Roofing & Building"
  description="House extensions in Leeds built by a roofing-led contractor: structure, tie-in and roof handled by one team, with the junction to the existing house done properly."
>
  <HeroText
    kicker="Construction / Leeds"
    heading="House extensions"
    lede="The hardest part of an extension is not the new walls. It is where new meets old: the structural tie-in, the roof junction, the flashings and the damp detailing. We build extensions from the trade that gets those details right."
  />

  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block-start: var(--space-4)">
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
        { label: 'Construction', href: '/construction/' },
        { label: 'Extensions' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What we take on</h2>
      <p>
        Single and two-storey extensions, garage conversions with new roofs over, and
        the structural carpentry that goes with them: joists, roof structures, dormers
        and openings. Where a project needs trades we do not carry ourselves, we work
        with people we know and stand behind the whole job.
      </p>
      <h2>Why a roofing-led builder</h2>
      <p>
        Most extension problems that show up two winters later are roof and weathering
        problems: a valley that ponds, an abutment flashed with sealant instead of lead,
        a flat junction that should have been pitched. Those are the details we do every
        day. Building the extension underneath them means nobody has to hand the
        critical part to somebody else.
      </p>
      <h2>How it runs</h2>
      <p>
        We price from your drawings or measure up with you, agree a written scope and
        programme, and keep the site tidy and the neighbours on side while we work. You
        deal with the same people from first visit to handover.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EvidenceGallery categories={['extensions', 'dormers']} heading="Extension work" />

  <CtaBand
    title="Extending your home?"
    note="Send us the drawings if you have them, or just describe what you want to do."
  />
</Base>
